# 1. Executive Summary

During the assessment, a **Web Cache Poisoning** vulnerability was identified due to the unsafe use of a client-controlled cookie (`fehost`).

The application reflected the value of this cookie directly into a JavaScript object embedded in the homepage. Because the caching layer did not include the `fehost` cookie as part of the cache key, an attacker could poison the cache with a malicious JavaScript payload that would subsequently be delivered to other users.

By injecting a carefully crafted payload into the cookie value, arbitrary JavaScript execution was achieved in the browsers of users requesting the poisoned page.

